  "stdout": "{\"action_authorized\": false, \"claims\": [{\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"claim_ceiling\": \"Multiple same-repository source-inspected cases; one PR #704 exact-head `context-for` consumer passed, but repeated agent benefit was not measured\", \"observed_revisions\": [\"2026-11-01\", \"2026-11-02\"], \"scope\": \"Historical source-to-context anchor assessments within Sensemaking-skills, not independent-agent cognition or cross-repository proof\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\": \"1acb7144f7dbef20166609ade88f4cf76c583be605b7cb8735b94374ed2f3cef\", \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-longitudinal-lesson-reentry.md\": \"efba1831ea71074723ec069ff029e09537930d3db5bcdc33e7333b7432804820\", \"docs/normal-use/graph-decision-context-strategic-comparison-2026-11-01.md\": \"636dffbee1e03fc72ea1633a0f3b460a1bc13f0fe7a8a0b824743592db93260a\", \"docs/normal-use/graph-reentry-prospective-guidance-2026-11-01.md\": \"37ac2ed3650949d0712eba7e23a5c7a6e6db5abf83758a3869596bbd8d457ea2\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"observed\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\", \"file:docs/normal-use/graph-decision-context-strategic-comparison-2026-11-01.md\", \"file:docs/normal-use/graph-reentry-prospective-guidance-2026-11-01.md\", \"file:docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-longitudinal-lesson-reentry.md\"], \"id\": \"incident:source-context-link-gaps-20261102\", \"kind\": \"incident\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"Across several source-reviewed Sensemaking edits in 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-02, file-first semantic context lacked a relevant ownership or history/decision link even though the underlying Skill guidance or historical lessons existed in original sources. PRs #691, #697, #701 and #704 used reviewed graph corrections rather than new query algorithms.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"operationalized_by\": \"Not operationalized by a new check. The guard is unchanged; non-ASCII glyphs were replaced in the three scripts' console-reachable report text. scripts/workflow-runtime.py was not assessed for console-reachable text.\", \"scope\": \"Source inspection and a stdout-encoding probe on one Windows host at 0b1df456. The two scripts were not executed (local test-runner execution is withheld by the construction policy). Whether later agents apply this lesson is NOT TESTED.\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"scripts/analyze-run-failures.py\": \"7f5c1908d50aab9be54583a291d9b8bdad40ac1217f6f21f3a118ae837048f45\", \"scripts/portfolio-orchestrator.py\": \"bdfcd6e3a5c79d0b620a35a6e0814a5b12c43325a22a5a9a24e41093598db7cf\", \"scripts/test-validators.py\": \"2797aceb42bdffb8f4f5d9fcfc711fc8886fe0308b7cc11e6c56e2b39de624b3\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/cli.py\": \"917065d4dca84f16ae4a98ce390c6cb470ef4954996677ad7dac1a1f00db935e\", \"tests/test_console_output_ascii_only.py\": \"9a3d0cde3c37318c12efefb276a1f85fee4060573a572b5f0045a866e24c29c4\"}, \"staleness_condition\": \"Stale when the guard learns to follow data flow into print(), when scripts/ gains an escape layer, or when the named print paths change.\"}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"CLAUDE.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"observed\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:tests/test_console_output_ascii_only.py\", \"file:scripts/test-validators.py\", \"file:scripts/analyze-run-failures.py\", \"file:scripts/portfolio-orchestrator.py\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/cli.py\"], \"id\": \"lesson:console-guard-literal-print-arguments-only\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"The ASCII console guard (tests/test_console_output_ascii_only.py) inspects only string literals written directly inside print() calls, so non-ASCII text that reaches print() through a variable passes it. On this Windows host a redirected stdout is cp1252, and printing U+2705 raises UnicodeEncodeError (probed). scripts/test-validators.py and scripts/analyze-run-failures.py printed report text that carried such glyphs, and only the cli.py main() entry point escapes unencodable output, so scripts/ entrypoints depend on ASCII source discipline alone.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"claim_ceiling\": \"Source-grounded guidance, not a claim that semantic changes can currently be detected automatically\", \"scope\": \"Source-grounded interpretation hygiene; integrated PR #561 implements additive classification of indexed record differences without automatic truth\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/semantic-steward-workspace-impact-2026-10-21.md\": \"4e30e7ded4ac83b455fb9cf0afde4d14fb859d8cd0cb866c1d42c29fa07b19f6\", \"docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\": \"b2d4d693c587a29cad2d0daf9c1fc874c9717fdc2e0183bf7136417bde8cc72b\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_sources.py\": \"b8e561604083bf3fa24a96d5a570ae91d8e35d15de24e60331d32fd0b988e3a8\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_store.py\": \"5b0108f96c25681330a9a25c3d3b0aaad25e83c96532fbd3af9e30882be36100\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/semantic-steward-workspace-impact-2026-10-21.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/semantic-steward-workspace-impact-2026-10-21.md\", \"file:docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_sources.py\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_store.py\"], \"id\": \"lesson:distinguish-provenance-content-and-meaning\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"Distinguish whole-file provenance drift, changes to individual authored record fields, changes to independently cited evidence, and source-verified changes in architectural meaning before concluding that a reviewed knowledge claim was revised.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"scope\": \"Historical pilot quality finding; no inference about all future packs\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/adr/0030-target-repository-grounding.md\": \"26454ca30a40ff5521efe933c59f4d3634d297a2719e8cefa22e6c97a6d4fdd4\", \"docs/normal-use/grounding-pack-build-001.md\": \"0d0c6f3bce8bc8cba3ba50653de635d4b83895597fab3e13e25d282c05d1fbe8\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"policy\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/adr/0030-target-repository-grounding.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/grounding-pack-build-001.md\"], \"id\": \"lesson:grounding-waiver\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"The first target Grounding Pack required corrections to 20% of a ten-line spot check; acceptance was by explicit owner waiver, not a passing quality sample.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"claim_ceiling\": \"Observed on one scratch setup-skills install; hosted or remote Skill surfaces are not covered by the file probe. The probe's default root is ~/.agents/skills, not the Claude Code root ~/.claude/skills; a Claude Code install is verified only when --installed-dir names its root, and a verdict covers only the root probed.\", \"decision_changed\": \"Whether a host's installed Sensemaking Skill can be reported as current after a merge.\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"INSTALLATION.md\": \"be41d60b781f2ec6b8cb1b5c5212e6a2a9d8c9267a6fc731d0c64b1cc37a528e\", \"scripts/probe_skill_distribution.py\": \"30f78f14c9d366402c12a3db55841d8ebec41e68409173c05e8c88a67d43235a\", \"scripts/repo_probes.py\": \"2b11492be55cfee81b128723bb5c5abc8f9f8f6e81b6041af1cf5f90f28764a6\", \"skills/using-sensemaking/SKILL.md\": \"62bd38d2f7522e0e14ef7bff6678125b12c964f7374da4a2f26aeead2af8c529\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"code\", \"authority_ref\": \"scripts/repo_probes.py\", \"epistemic_status\": \"observed\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:scripts/repo_probes.py\", \"file:scripts/probe_skill_distribution.py\", \"file:INSTALLATION.md\", \"file:skills/using-sensemaking/SKILL.md\"], \"id\": \"lesson:installed-skill-currency-includes-references\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"An installed Skill copy is current only if its references match as well as its SKILL.md: the compact using-sensemaking core loads load-bearing rules from references on demand, so a matching entrypoint with stale references changes agent behavior.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"claim_ceiling\": \"Context-qualified interpretation of one observed hosted caller failure. No cross-repository transfer, causal cognitive improvement or general method superiority established.\", \"revisit_when\": \"A later reviewed PR consumer uses a different comparison question, or actual normal use establishes this lesson is misleading, noisy or stale.\", \"scope\": \"PR-scoped review consumers with potentially diverged branches; does not change workspace-review-context's explicit arbitrary revision-pair semantics.\", \"source_sha256\": {\".github/workflows/semantic-context-reentry.yml\": \"5aa5c0ca0bd0d9c43261d9cbf9b6797a7ea7129d64fc805cc7876c45fd8f05a7\", \".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-12-scl-pr-review-baseline-feedback.md\": \"3110344448c4e3af201f6902aeaa55d71506e58f31da576a2935312e95b20f00\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/workspace_knowledge.py\": \"14f1a65f8cbbf15362a62758c735babd4314b1382b3f0f71934fa1f0723dc3a2\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-12-scl-pr-review-baseline-feedback.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/2026-11-12-scl-pr-review-baseline-feedback.md\", \"file:.github/workflows/semantic-context-reentry.yml\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/workspace_knowledge.py\"], \"id\": \"lesson:pr-review-merge-base-is-scope-evidence\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"When a PR-review consumer needs the PR change set, compare the topic head against its Git merge base with the target branch, not the moving base tip. Record the actual comparison refs and reconcile the reported changed paths with the PR's file set before interpreting source-overlap results; intentional arbitrary two-tree comparisons are different legitimate questions.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"scope\": \"One source-grounded bug class; whether later independent agents use this lesson remains NOT TESTED\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/semantic-stewardship-episode-a-2026-10-15.md\": \"cf166411369d83691b18b69bace183f508dc219eca45fad4bf9e8dc7c42b6239\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/semantic-stewardship-episode-a-2026-10-15.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/semantic-stewardship-episode-a-2026-10-15.md\"], \"id\": \"lesson:query-completeness-is-evidence\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"When a limited historical or change query silently reports completeness, absence of entries can be mistaken for absence of evidence; communicate omissions and totals before treating the result as architectural context.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"scope\": \"One calibration in one harness and CLI version; makes no claim about other tool sets, other hosts or cognitive benefit\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-15-harness-calibration-c2.md\": \"f6c84d8f6dad826cd4b47a960c21a46edd9b488e62e2bbd0a2e7c0072546f149\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-15-harness-calibration-c2.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/2026-11-15-harness-calibration-c2.md\"], \"id\": \"lesson:safe-mode-alone-does-not-confine-file-reads\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"Excluding instructions, memory and Skills with a safe mode does not confine file reading. A fixed-method arm that has any read tool also needs an explicit read restriction, such as --restricted with an explicit tool allowlist, before its reads can be limited to its working directory. This narrows the remedy named in lesson:subagent-inherits-ambient-context; it does not replace that lesson.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"decision_changed\": \"Whether an audit run from a hand-made clone can be trusted, and why --temporary-checkout materializes a worktree rather than a clone\", \"scope\": \"Observed on one Windows host on 2026-11-10, auditing an index of commit 53b667c1 at commit baaec6b9: 442 of 442 records reported changed from a clone made under the system default core.autocrlf=true, with and without --temporary-checkout, against 139 of 442 from a worktree of the repository. An independent reviewer reproduced both counts. Other conversions (filters, working-tree-encoding) not probed\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\": \"b2d4d693c587a29cad2d0daf9c1fc874c9717fdc2e0183bf7136417bde8cc72b\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_store.py\": \"5b0108f96c25681330a9a25c3d3b0aaad25e83c96532fbd3af9e30882be36100\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"observed\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_store.py\"], \"id\": \"lesson:separate-clone-changes-audited-bytes\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"A separate clone is not a neutral clean checkout for knowledge-audit. Source fingerprints are taken from checked-out bytes, after any line-ending conversion, so in a clone made under another core.autocrlf setting cited text files read as changed. A temporary worktree of the same repository uses that repository's configuration and checks out the same bytes as its ordinary checkout; the flag does not make differently configured clones agree.\"}, {\"attributes\": {\"authority_verified\": false, \"claim_ceiling\": \"Source-grounded local lesson from several overlapping repository episodes, with independent repeated benefit and transfer NOT_ASSESSED\", \"revised\": \"2026-11-10: context-for gained relevance_candidates (capability and citation routes), the condition this record named in revisit_when. The earlier wording said unanchored history was not reachable; it is now listed as a candidate, and anchoring is still what makes it context. The earlier text is in Git history before this change.\", \"revisit_when\": \"If context-for changes how anchors or candidates are selected again, or a fresh independent agent demonstrates a misleading or non-useful application, source-check and revise this lesson without deleting the original incident\", \"scope\": \"Sensemaking source-file context-for mechanism only; not a universal directive to add more links or a demonstration that an agent applies this rule\", \"source_sha256\": {\".sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\": \"fc5b722ed15d986b3fc1114e7cd43f52584e10e8d7118d43d91b3db3c9ef2900\", \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\": \"1acb7144f7dbef20166609ade88f4cf76c583be605b7cb8735b94374ed2f3cef\", \"docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\": \"b2d4d693c587a29cad2d0daf9c1fc874c9717fdc2e0183bf7136417bde8cc72b\", \"skills/repository-semantic-steward/references/recall.md\": \"60dbf1f9a5aa2307227041d17a9c38b927f68ee758c2b6512a128613dd65a280\", \"src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_architecture.py\": \"36212487c0f922351a04e18629effbd0f6c7b14f5aa305da858c94290f8d0e73\"}}, \"authority_kind\": \"document\", \"authority_ref\": \"docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\", \"epistemic_status\": \"declared\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"file:docs/normal-use/2026-11-02-cross-episode-source-reentry-learning.md\", \"file:src/sensemaking_skills/semantic_architecture/knowledge_architecture.py\", \"file:skills/repository-semantic-steward/references/recall.md\", \"file:docs/semantic-architecture/persistent-knowledge-cli.md\"], \"id\": \"lesson:source-anchored-context-reentry\", \"kind\": \"lesson\", \"source_ref\": \"file:.sensemaking/knowledge/stewardship.json\", \"statement\": \"For Sensemaking's file-first `context-for` retrieval, a record counts as context for a file a component owns only when reviewed `owned_paths` plus explicit component/rule-to-history or decision relations connect it. A record held on a capability the owner implements, or one that cites the file, is listed under `relevance_candidates` with applicability NOT_ESTABLISHED: visible, not anchored. Before adding a new query type, inspect those anchors and original sources; missing graph context is not evidence that the engineering history is absent.\"}], \"code\": \"SEMANTIC_KNOWLEDGE_QUERY\", \"explicit_limits\": [\"This is a bounded projection of tracked sources; missing claims/edges mean NOT ASSESSED, not absent.\", \"Declared authorities, authored edges and cited tests are source claims, not automatically verified truth.\", \"Observed code imports are syntax only; neither runtime dependency nor architectural significance is inferred.\", \"No query or graph relationship authorizes a product decision, merge, deployment or release.\", \"Knowledge records are declared/observed at the indexed revision, NOT semantic truth or action authority.\"], \"operation\": \"search\", \"relations\": [], \"repository\": \"sensemaking-skills\", \"search_hit_total\": 13, \"search_mode\": \"explicit_terms_any\", \"semantic_truth_established\": false, \"source_scope\": [\"tracked Grounding Pack lines\", \"tracked ADR title/status\", \"tracked authored knowledge JSON\"], \"target_ref\": \"b7ce9e699d63d637c9798da6b15db325a02f7ce8\", \"truncated\": true, \"workspace_context\": {\"current_head\": \"b7ce9e699d63d637c9798da6b15db325a02f7ce8\", \"external_filter_commands_disabled_count\": 0, \"head_matches_indexed_ref\": true, \"indexed_ref\": \"b7ce9e699d63d637c9798da6b15db325a02f7ce8\", \"modified_tracked_count\": 0, \"source_alignment_not_semantic_truth\": true, \"submodule_worktrees_not_assessed\": true, \"uncommitted_changes_not_indexed\": false, \"untracked_count\": 0, \"worktree_clean\": true}}\r\n",
